#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_dir.rst:15
msgid "``build_dir``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_dir.rst:18
msgid ""
"**PLEASE DO NOT EDIT FILES IN THIS FOLDER**. PlatformIO will overwrite your "
"changes on the next build. **THIS IS A CACHE DIRECTORY**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_dir.rst:21
msgid ""
"Type: ``DirPath`` | Multiple: ``No`` | Default: \":ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_workspace_dir`/build\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_dir.rst:23
msgid ""
"*PlatformIO Build System* uses this folder for project environments to store "
"compiled object files, static libraries, firmwares and other cached "
"information. It allows PlatformIO to build source code extremely fast!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_dir.rst:28
msgid ""
"*You can delete this folder without any risk!* If you modify :ref:"
"`projectconf`, then PlatformIO will remove this folder automatically. It "
"will be created on the next build operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_dir.rst:32
msgid ""
"This option can also be configured by the global environment variable :"
"envvar:`PLATFORMIO_BUILD_DIR`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_dir.rst:36
msgid ""
"If you have any problems with building your project environments which are "
"defined in :ref:`projectconf`, then **TRY TO DELETE** this folder. In this "
"situation you will remove all cached files without any risk. Also, you can "
"use \"clean\" target for :option:`pio run --target` command."
msgstr ""
